246
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:44,340
Honey, it's not pushy. He gave her his home number.

247
00:14:44,500 --> 00:14:48,090
Wha...? He gave you his home number, as in, like, to his home?

248
00:14:48,260 --> 00:14:52,140
Yeah. And you don't mind if I call, because you only want good things for me.

249
00:14:52,300 --> 00:14:56,140
That's right, good things. That is what I said.

250
00:14:58,680 --> 00:15:03,100
Ahem. Hello, Mark? Hi, it's Rachel Green.

251
00:15:04,980 --> 00:15:09,360
Ha, ha. Oh, no. Don't you apologize.

252
00:15:09,530 --> 00:15:10,610
Yeah, I'll hold.

253
00:15:11,360 --> 00:15:12,570
He left my number at work.

254
00:15:12,740 --> 00:15:16,280
He was gonna get it, but he was helping his niece with her report on the pioneers.

255
00:15:16,450 --> 00:15:19,950
That is so made up.

256
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:24,290
Yeah. Oh, my God. Tomorrow? That's... No, it's perfect.

257
00:15:24,460 --> 00:15:28,380
Oh, God. Thank you so much. Great. Bye.

258
00:15:28,550 --> 00:15:30,010
Oh! I got the interview.

259
00:15:30,170 --> 00:15:31,930
There you go.

260
00:15:32,090 --> 00:15:35,220
He even offered to meet me for lunch and prep me for it.

261
00:15:35,390 --> 00:15:37,140
- Oh, that is amazing.     - Yeah.

262
00:15:37,310 --> 00:15:40,600
Well, if I know Mark, and I think I do...

263
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:44,730
- ...I'd expect nothing less.     - I gotta figure out what I'm gonna wear.

264
00:15:44,900 --> 00:15:48,320
High collar and baggy pants say, "I'm a pro."

265
00:15:49,030 --> 00:15:51,440
Yeah, right. Okay, I'll see you guys later.

266
00:15:51,610 --> 00:15:52,650
Okay.

267
00:15:52,820 --> 00:15:54,910
You go get them.

268
00:15:55,070 --> 00:15:58,160
What did I do to you? Did I hurt you in some way?

269
00:15:58,990 --> 00:16:02,330
- What?     - "Why don't you call him?"

270
00:16:02,500 --> 00:16:04,830
Well, thank you very much. Now he's gonna prep her.

271
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:10,210
You know, prep her, as in what you do before you surgically remove the boyfriend.

272
00:16:10,380 --> 00:16:11,630
Are you crazy?

273
00:16:11,840 --> 00:16:15,260
Oh, am I? Am I? Am I out of my mind? Am I losing my senses?

274
00:16:17,100 --> 00:16:20,310
This dreamy guy is taking my girlfriend out for a meal.

275
00:16:20,470 --> 00:16:22,520
Ross, you know, this isn't even about you.

276
00:16:22,730 --> 00:16:25,440
This is about Rachel and something happening for her.

277
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:27,360
Even if you're right.

278
00:16:27,520 --> 00:16:30,690
What if he wants to sleep with her? Does that mean he gets to?

279
00:16:30,860 --> 00:16:32,820
- No, but...     - I mean, don't you trust her?

280
00:16:33,030 --> 00:16:34,240
Well, yeah...

281
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:36,950
Then get over yourself. Grow up.

282
00:16:41,160 --> 00:16:43,250
You grow up.

283
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:57,680
This tiramisu is excellent.

284
00:16:57,850 --> 00:17:01,140
- Did you make it, Mary Angela?     - No, I did.

285
00:17:02,390 --> 00:17:04,060
Well, it's yummy.

286
00:17:05,100 --> 00:17:08,940
So, uh, Mary Angela, do you like it?

287
00:17:09,110 --> 00:17:11,360
Of course. It's her favorite.

288
00:17:13,530 --> 00:17:15,400
So, um, hmm...

289
00:17:15,570 --> 00:17:18,360
Mary Angela, what's your second favorite?

290
00:17:18,570 --> 00:17:20,160
More of Grandma's tiramisu.

291
00:17:20,330 --> 00:17:23,120
Oh, would you just please...

292
00:17:24,580 --> 00:17:26,710
...give me your recipe, because this is great.

293
00:17:26,870 --> 00:17:28,580
It's top-notch.

294
00:17:28,750 --> 00:17:31,880
- That dies with me.     - So will I.

295
00:17:33,550 --> 00:17:35,720
Excuse yourself and go to the bathroom.

296
00:17:35,880 --> 00:17:38,510
Oh, no, I was just squinting. That doesn't mean anything.

297
00:17:38,680 --> 00:17:40,220
Just do it.

298
00:17:45,770 --> 00:17:48,140
Will you excuse me? I have to, um...

299
00:17:59,490 --> 00:18:00,950
Hey...

300
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:03,530
Finally. I thought we'd never be alone.

301
00:18:03,700 --> 00:18:04,990
Can I just tell you something?

302
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:07,750
I have not stopped thinking about you since the party.

303
00:18:10,210 --> 00:18:13,960
Look, I may have jumped the gun here. Whoa.

304
00:18:15,960 --> 00:18:17,800
I just got out of a relationship.

305
00:18:17,970 --> 00:18:21,930
And I'm not really in a... In a commitment kind of place.

306
00:18:22,100 --> 00:18:23,180
So? Me neither.

307
00:18:23,350 --> 00:18:26,680
God, Mary Angela was right. You do have the softest lips.

308
00:18:28,560 --> 00:18:32,310
- You're not Mary Angela?     - No. I'm Mary Therese.

309
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:34,820
This is so bad.

310
00:18:34,980 --> 00:18:37,820
If you're not Mary Angela, then who is?

311
00:18:38,030 --> 00:18:39,740
I am.

312
00:18:40,780 --> 00:18:42,990
Oh, it's so bad.

313
00:18:43,160 --> 00:18:46,830
- Joey!     - No Joey. No Joey. No Joey.

314
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,160
- Joey.     - What's going on?

315
00:18:50,210 --> 00:18:52,330
You're it. Now run and hide.

316
00:18:53,630 --> 00:18:54,670
It's no big deal.

317
00:18:54,840 --> 00:18:58,380
Chandler was just kissing me because he thought I was Mary Angela.

318
00:18:58,550 --> 00:19:01,720
What? How could you do that? How could you think she was Mary Angela?

319
00:19:01,890 --> 00:19:04,850
I wasn't sure which one Mary Angela was.

320
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:07,720
Look, I'm sorry, okay?

321
00:19:07,890 --> 00:19:10,980
I was really drunk, and you guys all look really similar.

322
00:19:11,190 --> 00:19:12,230
I say punch him, Joey.

323
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:14,060
- Yeah, punch him.     - Yeah, kick him.

324
00:19:14,230 --> 00:19:15,520
We should all calm down...

325
00:19:15,690 --> 00:19:18,900
...because, you know, your brother's not gonna punch me.

326
00:19:19,070 --> 00:19:20,990
Are you?

327
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:22,950
Well, that is usually what I would do.

328
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:25,490
But I never thought you'd be on the receiving end.

329
00:19:25,660 --> 00:19:27,330
How could you do this?

330
00:19:27,490 --> 00:19:29,870
Joey, if you wanna punch me, go ahead. I deserve it.

331
00:19:30,040 --> 00:19:34,420
But I just want you to know that I would never soberly hurt you or your family.

332
00:19:34,630 --> 00:19:36,500
You're my best friend.

333
00:19:36,670 --> 00:19:39,420
And I would never do anything like this ever again.

334
00:19:41,300 --> 00:19:42,430
So what?

335
00:19:42,590 --> 00:19:45,510
- I say punch him. Punch him.     - Yeah, punch him.

336
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:49,350
- Come on, punch him.     - No. No. I'm not gonna punch Chandler.

337
00:19:49,930 --> 00:19:51,810
- I'll do it.     - No, you won't.

338
00:19:52,350 --> 00:19:55,020
Look, he knows he did a terrible thing, and I believe him.

339
00:19:55,190 --> 00:19:57,900
He's sorry. But you got one more apology to make.

340
00:19:58,070 --> 00:20:00,740
All right? You gotta apologize to Mary Angela.

341
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:03,780
- Okay. Absolutely. You got it.     - All right.

342
00:20:13,540 --> 00:20:15,460
- Cookie, now you can punch him.     - What?

343
00:20:23,930 --> 00:20:24,970
- Hey.     - Hi.

344
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:26,260
What are you doing here?

345
00:20:26,430 --> 00:20:29,180
You know, this building's on my paper route, so...

346
00:20:29,390 --> 00:20:31,020
- Oh. Hi.     - Hi.

347
00:20:31,180 --> 00:20:32,230
How did it go?

348
00:20:32,390 --> 00:20:35,060
Oh, well, the woman I interviewed with was pretty tough...

349
00:20:35,230 --> 00:20:37,230
...but, you know, thank God Mark coached me.

350
00:20:37,400 --> 00:20:40,440
Once I started talking about the fall line, she got all happy.

351
00:20:40,610 --> 00:20:43,490
- I'm so proud of you.     - Me too.

352
00:20:44,280 --> 00:20:45,570
Listen, I'm, uh...

353
00:20:46,740 --> 00:20:51,080
I'm sorry I've been so crazy and jealous and...

354
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:53,580
It's just, I like you a lot, so...

355
00:20:53,750 --> 00:20:54,790
I know.

356
00:20:54,960 --> 00:20:56,000
- Yeah?     - Yeah.

357
00:20:56,170 --> 00:20:57,210
- Rachel.     - Yeah?

358
00:20:57,380 --> 00:20:58,630
- Hi. Hi.     - Hi, Mark.

359
00:20:58,790 --> 00:21:02,130
I just talked to Joanna, and she loves you. You got it. You got the job.

360
00:21:02,300 --> 00:21:03,670
- What?     - Oh! I did?

361
00:21:03,840 --> 00:21:04,920
Yes.

362
00:21:05,090 --> 00:21:06,300
Oh, my God!

363
00:21:06,470 --> 00:21:09,010
Congratulations...

364
00:21:13,980 --> 00:21:15,520
So, Phoebe.

365
00:21:15,690 --> 00:21:16,810
How was your date?

366
00:21:16,980 --> 00:21:19,020
Oh, well, you know. Ha, ha.

367
00:21:19,190 --> 00:21:21,650
Yeah, I do know.

368
00:21:21,820 --> 00:21:23,230
Ick. You were eavesdropping?

369
00:21:23,400 --> 00:21:27,280
Eavesdropping? Pheebs, the ceiling tiles were falling down.

370
00:21:28,990 --> 00:21:30,490
Oh, I'm sorry.

371
00:21:30,660 --> 00:21:35,960
But I really like this guy, and I think he really happens to like me.

372
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:45,840
Maybe he's just jumping on a pogo stick and he really likes it.

373
00:21:49,550 --> 00:21:51,600
Maybe the pogo stick likes it too.

374
00:21:53,430 --> 00:21:56,180
All right, that's it. He cannot do this to Phoebe.

375
00:21:56,350 --> 00:21:59,600
This guy's gonna get the butt-kicking of a lifetime.

376
00:21:59,770 --> 00:22:02,270
But is he a big guy?

377
00:22:02,440 --> 00:22:03,570
We'll all go. Come on.

378
00:22:03,730 --> 00:22:06,440
- Thanks, you guys. Thank you.     - Don't worry.

379
00:22:06,610 --> 00:22:10,160
God. I hope they kick his ass.

380
00:22:10,370 --> 00:22:11,820
Honey, I'm sorry.

381
00:22:11,990 --> 00:22:13,660
You know, if it's any consolation...

382
00:22:13,830 --> 00:22:16,660
...he really did sound like he was having more fun with you.

